// Title: Suspicious Creation with Colorcpl
// Sigma ID: e15b518d-b4ce-4410-a9cd-501f23ce4a18
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-21 | Modified: 2023-01-05
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564
// Description: Once executed, colorcpl.exe will copy the arbitrary file to
//   c:\windows\system32\spool\drivers\color\
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/eral4m/status/1480468728324231172?s=20
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_colorcpl.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\colorcpl.exe" and (not((FolderPath endswith ".icm" or FolderPath endswith ".gmmp" or FolderPath endswith ".cdmp" or FolderPath endswith ".camp")))
